    {
      "id": "r20261028-a02",
      "title": "The Power of Micro-Volunteering",
      "level": "Menengah atas",
      "min": 4,
      "body": [
        "Many people want to help their communities, but they do not have hours of free time. This is why micro-volunteering is becoming popular: doing good in just a few minutes.",
        "Micro-volunteering means doing small tasks that help others. For example, you can translate a document for a charity during your lunch break, identify plants in photos for scientists while waiting for the bus, or record your voice reading a story for blind children. All of this can be done from your phone, in under thirty minutes.",
        "These small actions may seem tiny, but together they are powerful. When thousands of people each give fifteen minutes, charities get hundreds of hours of free help. Micro-volunteering shows us that you do not need a lot of time to make a difference. You just need to start."
      ],
      "gloss": {
        "communities": "komunitas",
        "charity": "badan amal",
        "identify": "mengidentifikasi",
        "lunch break": "istirahat makan siang",
        "blind": "buta",
        "tiny": "kecil",
        "difference": "perbedaan"
      },
